  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Design and implementation of policies to tackle informality and protect workers improved</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Between 2010 and 2022, the infrastructure of the national Economic and Social Council (ESC) was established, significantly enhancing its role in shaping economic and social policies. The ILO has provided technical assistance to the Government to establish a mechanism for the amicable settlement of labour disputes (ASLD), but its outreach remains limited. Previous ILO support has contributed to an advanced draft Labour Relations Law, an adopted Action Plan for the ESC, and an Action Plan on ASLD. 

Labour and industrial relations reform is a key part of the Government&#x2019;s agenda as North Macedonia advances toward EU accession. The ILO&#x2019;s strategy aligns with recommendations from the Committee on the Application of Standards (CAS) following the 2023 International Labour Conference, which called on the Government to ensure full compliance with Convention No. 98 on the right to organize and collective bargaining. The ILO supports the implementation of recommendations from the ILO Direct Contacts Mission (DCM) to assist the Government and social partners in addressing CAS considerations and advancing labour law reforms. 
To strengthen collective bargaining and the amicable settlement of labour disputes, the ILO promotes ASLD by conducting a legal analysis of the ASLD Law, facilitating ESC working group meetings to prepare amendments, developing a Code of Conduct for conciliators and arbiters, organizing an ITC-ILO training on ASLD systems, and preparing promotional materials. Additionally, the ILO supports collective bargaining through technical input on the draft Labour Relations Law, an analysis of selected collective agreements,  and the development of promotional materials. These efforts will contribute to a more effective and inclusive industrial relations system in North Macedonia.</narrative>
  </description>
